executionContract.intendedBehavior:
A PowerShell worker or QA seat can carry a launch outage over from an earlier legacy iteration of the same wrapper process. On that seat's first verified-local VM-route iteration, right after Invoke-MoeVerifiedLocalGate, moe-agent.ps1 now ends the outage:
- it prints the sh twin's [launch-outage] VM-route line;
- it posts one best-effort #general line;
- it resets the launch-failure streak, its backoff and the four outage variables.
The pre-flight then calls claim_next_task again, marked executionRoute vm. Before the fix, the outage suppressed every claim while the VM route turned each launch probe into a no-launch. Legacy, observe and unreadable seats are unchanged.
